#12926
Beneath a Mighty Rock~
   You squeeze through a narrow passage and into a larger chamber beneath the
massive, black rock. The walls here are glassy stone, carefully carved to
create space to mine the underside of the rock. Here and there, the stone is
marred by long slices where portals have dug into it over many years.
Commands: return
~
cei 0 0 12920
D8
~
0 12921
E
passage narrow~
   The passage back up to the surface of the crater is tight, but you can just
squeeze through.
~
E
chamber~
The chamber beneath the rock is much more spacious than the passage.
~
E
rock craggy~
The metallic rock above you has been mined for ore; there's still a lot left.
~
E
walls grooves~
The walls are glassy, grooved where they've been carved to make the chamber.
~
E
glassy stone~
   Much of the stone here is glassy, as if it was once heated to a tremendous
temperature.
~
E
scars~
The walls and floors are scarred with grooves created by many magical portals.
~
E
floor down~
The floor is rock.
~
E
up meteorite~
Above you is the great meteorite nestled in the crater.
~
